    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d741">

                <pb facs="0923" n="915" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg915"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.94/1284: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-28T14:00:00+03:00">February 28,
                            1941—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>389. Following has been sent to Tokyo:</p>
                <p>“I very much appreciate your 321, of February 27, 1 p.m., as I am now convinced
                    that my Japanese colleague has been entirely [accurate?] and sincere during the
                    past 2 or 3 months in his statements to me concerning the status from time to
                    time of the Soviet-Japanese negotiations and that I may in consequence place
                    reliance on any further information that I may obtain from him.[”]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
